function renderDailyRows(){const headers=$('daily-rows').closest('table').tHead.rows[0].cells;headers[1].textContent=activeBranch?'Parent path mean weight (kg)':'Baseline mean weight (kg)';headers[2].textContent=activeBranch?'New branch mean weight (kg)':'Intervention mean weight (kg)';const host=$('daily-rows');host.replaceChildren(...latest.comparison.rows.map(row=>{const tr=document.createElement('tr');const values=[row.day,fmt(row.referenceWeight),fmt(row.scenarioWeight),`${row.scenarioWeight-row.referenceWeight>=0?'+':''}${fmt(row.scenarioWeight-row.referenceWeight)}`,fmt(row.scenarioPastureKgDM,0)];for(const value of values){const td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=String(value);tr.append(td);}return tr;}));}
function renderProvenance(){const node=$('provenance-details');const lineage=activeBranch?`This branch starts from ${activeBranch.sourceArm==='reference'?'the baseline':'the intervention'} at day ${activeBranch.checkpointDay}; the checkpoint was deterministically restored from the parent manifest (SHA-256 ${activeBranch.checkpointSha256}). The parent manifest seed is ${activeBranch.seed}; the declared change is ${activeBranch.branchConfig.supplement} kg DM/animal/day.`:`Both arms were cloned from the same snapshot with seed ${latest.manifest.seed}; only ${latest.manifest.factor} differs.`;node.innerHTML=`<ul><li>Model: ${latest.comparison.engineVersion}; executor: ${latest.execution.engineImplementation}.</li><li>${lineage}</li><li>The shared engine models illustrative feeding, hourly activity transitions, energy and thirst indices, pasture balance and illustrative cost. It is not independently validated as an animal-performance prediction.</li><li>Heat changes illustrative engine weather rules; this is not a validated thermal stress or heat-response model.</li><li>Initial weight variation comes from the seeded demo engine, not an observed Nellore cohort. Breed is metadata and does not change calculations.</li><li>Pasture stock is an internal paddock quantity. It is not transported from the biomass research models or from measured property inventory.</li><li>Transition reasons are deterministic demonstration rules. Generative-agent research and Perea grouped behavior results are not used to generate animal behavior.</li><li>No confidence probabilities or prediction intervals are produced. DMI per animal is unavailable. BR-CORTE Eq. 2.6 is not automatically connected because it requires externally supplied ADG; it does not predict ADG.</li></ul>`;}
